  "content": "A total of seven CVEs affecting Copilot and Azure AI Foundry highlighted the growing exposure that organizations face from AI tools, added Tyler Reguly, associate director of security R&D at Fortra. \"Are we aware of all our uses of AI?\" Reguly asked in an emailed statement, adding that 6% of the CVEs this month were AI-based. \"We know that number is only going to grow from here,\" he noted. \"What other instances of AI might be in use in your organization that are not backed by a company with a regular update schedule like Microsoft?\"",
